s = connect()
u = find_user(s, check["username"])
assert u, "STOP: missing employee"
groups = group_names(s, u["id"])
assert "Finance-Editors" not in groups, "STOP: prohibited grant exists"
print("HOLD IAM-X-202: approval is missing")
print("EDITOR GROUP PRESENT:", "Finance-Editors" in groups)
RUN / PERFORM:
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe work.py
EXPECTED RESULT:
HOLD IAM-X-202: approval is missing
EDITOR GROUP PRESENT: False
CHECK AGAINST THE ACTUAL RESULT:
No state-changing command is executed.
Rohit is still viewer-only.
Record HOLD and route for approval.
UNDERSTAND:
In IAM, refusing an unauthorized change is a real security action.
NEXT STEP / EVIDENCE:
After the no-change check, run .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe route_hold.py IAM-X-202 and verify the IAM-APPROVALS queue receipt.

